  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Angles measured in radians give clean formulas for arc length and sector area.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Radians",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\) radians. Arc length \\( s=r\\theta \\); sector area \\( A=\\tfrac12 r^{2}\\theta \\), with \\( \\theta \\) in radians.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Convert",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arc length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( s=r\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sector",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac12 r^{2}\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Full turn",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 2\\pi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the arc length when \\( r=5 \\) and \\( \\theta=\\tfrac{\\pi}{3} \\).</p>\\[ s=5\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Segment area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A sector OAB has radius 8 cm and angle \\(\\angle AOB=1.2\\) rad. Find the area of the minor segment cut off by chord AB.</p>\\[\\text{Sector area}=\\tfrac{1}{2}(8)^2(1.2)=38.4\\text{ cm}^2.\\]\\[\\text{Triangle area}=\\tfrac{1}{2}(8)^2\\sin(1.2)=32\\sin(1.2)\\approx29.56\\text{ cm}^2.\\]\\[\\text{Segment}=38.4-29.56\\approx8.84\\text{ cm}^2.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "The area of a sector is \\(54\\) cm² and its radius is 6 cm. Find the arc length.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Area \\(=\\tfrac{1}{2}r^2\\theta\\Rightarrow54=18\\theta\\Rightarrow\\theta=3\\) rad. Arc \\(=r\\theta=6\\times3=18\\) cm.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
